Vocab uses and redistributes data derived from the BHSA (Biblia Hebraica
Stuttgartensia Amstelodamensis), version 2021, by the Eep Talstra Centre for
Bible and Computer (ETCBC), Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam, which is licensed
under CC BY-NC 4.0 (https://github.com/ETCBC/bhsa). Vocab is licensed under
the same terms. Any use must give credit to the ETCBC and may not be commercial.

Vocab also includes the Greek New Testament (Nestle 1904) from the Text-Fabric
edition N1904 by the Center of Biblical Languages and Computing and the ETCBC
(MIT License, https://github.com/CenterBLC/N1904), based on MACULA Greek by
Clear Bible (CC BY 4.0, https://github.com/Clear-Bible/macula-greek), and Greek
glosses from Bible Online Learner by Ezer IT Consulting, used with permission
(https://github.com/EzerIT/BibleOL).

